           EOTL COMMUNICATION: PART ONE
 
There are various ways of communicating on EotL.  You can say, 
tell, whisper, channel, shout, and emote.  
 
When you use the command 'say bogleg!' (or "'bogleg!" which is 
effectively the same) everyone in the room where you use the 
command will see the following: Yourname says: bogleg!
 
The tell command allows you say something to a specific 
player who is not necessarily in the same room as you
in the following manner: 'tell hannah pleeze frob me!!'  
This command will tell the player Hannah, assuming that she's 
on and not net-dead, 'Yourname tells you: pleeze frob me!!'
 
You may also use the 'reply' to send a tell to the last person 
who told you.  For example...
 
Hannah tells you: No, I will not frob you.  Ever.  Leave me 
                  alone.
 
reply aww cmon i got goods ideas!11~!~!!
 
You tell Hannah: aww cmon i got goods ideas!11~!~!!
 
Also, if you substitute a '.' for the player's name, you will 
send a tell to the last person you told.  For example...
 
tell hannah y r u mad at me???
You tell Hannah: y r u mad at me???
tell . i'm sorry, pleeeze frob me????
You tell Hannah: i'm sorry, pleeze frob me????
 
The tell command can be used to tell multiple targets by 
typing 'tell player, player2, player3 message'
For example...
 
tell markus, hannah, minister whos in charge here?//???
You tell Markus, Hannah, and Minister: whos in charge here?//???
 
To reply to a group message, you must use 'reply -a message' 
or you will only tell to the first person in the group.
 
Whisper is similar to tell, in that people in the same room 
will not see the message.  But you may only whisper to someone 
in the same room.  The format is: 'whisper player message'
For example...
 
whisper hannah your my favoreet wizzie!
You whisper to Hannah: your my favoreet wizzie!
 
Emotes, or feelings, are used to convey feelings on the mud.  
EotL has over 1100 predefined emotes and that number is increasing 
rapidly.  They are used by typing the name of the emote (to
get a full list of emotes, type 'feelings').  For example...
Typing 'grin' will produce the message 'Yourname grins.' to 
the room you are currently in.  You may also customize certain 
feelings.  'grin happily' will produce the message 'Yourname 
grins happily.' in the room you are in.  Type 'help <emote>' 
to find out more about specific emotes.  If you can't find the 
emote you want among those already defined, you may type 
'emote <emote>' to produce the feeling you desire.  For 
example, 'emote fribbles!' will produce the message 'Yourname 
fribbles!' in the room you are in.
 
At a certain point, you will hear shouts.  Shouts are messages 
generally produced by wizzes that the whole mud can hear.  
Mortals, with a few rare exceptions, cannot shout.
 
Channels will be covered in the next lesson.           
